00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:21.880
So, first of all, basically

00:22:21.881 --> 00:22:24.555
if you look at the escape
analysis you mentioned,

00:22:24.556 --> 00:22:28.240
you are actually looking
at converting to

00:22:28.241 --> 00:22:30.070
stack allocation the objects

00:22:30.071 --> 00:22:31.410
used within that function, right?

00:22:31.411 --> 00:22:33.020
So, in our case, we are actually

00:22:33.021 --> 00:22:35.035
doing a whole program analysis.

00:22:35.036 --> 00:22:37.120
We are taking the entire program,

00:22:37.121 --> 00:22:41.300
and seeing how we can
actually reuse the objects.

00:22:41.301 --> 00:22:42.880
So, basically what we do is-

00:22:42.881 --> 00:22:45.310
&gt;&gt; Those techniques also
do good program analysis.

00:22:45.311 --> 00:22:47.380
Don't think they
