&gt;&gt; That can be your novelty.

00:23:03.736 --> 00:23:06.440
&gt;&gt; Okay. So, basically

00:23:06.990 --> 00:23:09.730
this is our entire
pipeline lifetime.

00:23:09.731 --> 00:23:16.930
So, first of all

00:23:16.931 --> 00:23:19.330
we only look at big objects

00:23:19.331 --> 00:23:22.180
like matrix and vector objects,
not primitive types.

00:23:22.181 --> 00:23:24.740
So, basically what we do is,

00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:32.780
let us say this is
the address line.

00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:38.795
Initially, what we do is we
actually create regions,

00:23:38.796 --> 00:23:43.230
so each region is
a contiguous block of memory.

00:23:43.231 --> 00:23:46.145
We actually allocate a separate
region for each object,

00:23:46.146 --> 00:23:48.755
then we try it and try to
optimize and merge regions.

00:23:48.756 --> 00:23:50.150
So actually our algorithm how it

00:23:50.151 --> 00:23:51.885
works till we reach
a fixed point,

00:23:51.886 --> 00:23:54.440
where no more
optimization is possible.

00:23:54.441 --> 00:23:57.795
So, let us say we
have another object,

00:23:57.796 --> 00:23:59.585
we have another object.

00:23:59.586 --> 00:24:06.010
This is the entire pipeline,

00:24:06.011 --> 00:24:08.215
one cycle of the pipeline.

00:24:08.216 --> 00:24:10.870
What we do is, so for example,

00:24:10.871 --> 00:24:14.750
let's say that, eraser?

00:24:17.010 --> 00:24:22.580
You cannot erase it. But in
our case, we can reallocate.

00:24:25.800 --> 00:24:29.960
Initially, we start with
separate addresses,

00:24:30.020 --> 00:24:34.250
and then we see here that

00:24:34.251 --> 00:24:37.890
this particular object does
not overlap with this-

00:24:37.891 --> 00:24:39.480
the lifetime does
not overlap with

00:24:39.481 --> 00:24:41.550
this object, then we reuse.

00:24:41.551 --> 00:24:44.935
So, we merge them
into a single region.

00:24:44.936 --> 00:24:48.000
So, now that region
has one block with

00:24:48.001 --> 00:24:51.715
this lifetime and another block
with this lifetime.

00:24:51.716 --> 00:24:54.000
Now, we have another block here,

00:24:54.001 --> 00:24:56.585
which are non-overlapping
lifetime with this,

00:24:56.586 --> 00:24:57.940
so we again merge it.

00:24:57.941 --> 00:25:00.245
So, now we have one block
with this much lifetime.

00:25:00.246 --> 00:25:02.860
We still have a remaining block
with- so we actually

00:25:02.861 --> 00:25:06.820
